 "final_message": "All 6 visible tests now pass. I fixed three bugs:\n\n1. **`money.format_cents`**: negative amounts were formatted with floor division and modulo on the signed value, so `-310` came out as `-$-4.90`. It now takes the absolute value before splitting into dollars and cents, giving `-$3.10`.\n2. **`parse.parse_date`**: month and day were swapped in the returned tuple. It now returns `(year, month, day)`.\n3. **`report.top_items`**: it sorted by total ascending. It now sorts by total descending, with ties broken by item name ascending, as the docstring says. `summary_line` uses it, so that is fixed too.",
